James sought assistance in drafting an introduction for a report section on the case for adaptation investment aimed at economic decision-makers, particularly Ministries of Finance. He outlined key points to include: benefits and costs of adaptation investment, conceptualization of avoided impacts, the triple dividend concept, distinctions between CapEx and OpEx as well as non-monetary costs, and additional benefits of increased resilience. In response, I provided a comprehensive draft that emphasized the economic rationale behind adaptation investments, explaining avoided impacts, detailing the triple dividend of prevention, stimulation, and co-benefits, and exploring the financial and non-financial impacts. The conclusion positioned adaptation as both an environmental necessity and an economic opportunity, aligning with sustainable development goals.

